> east
Kitchen
This is the kitchen of the white house. A table seems to have been used recently for the preparation of food. A passage leads to the west, and a dark staircase can be seen leading upward. To the east is a small window which is open.

You can see an elongated brown sack and a glass bottle here.

> take bottle
Taken.

> west
Living Room
This is the living room. There is a door to the east. To the west is a wooden door with strange gothic lettering, which appears to be nailed shut. A trophy case takes up one corner of the room. A large oriental rug lies to one side of the room, moved away from the trap door it once covered.

You can see an incense, a skeleton key, a guidebook, a matchbook, a large brochure, a wrench, a screwdriver, a trunk, a brass lantern, a brass bell, a black book, a burned-out candles, and a sharp stick here.

> open trap door
The trap trap door is already open.

> down
Cellar
This is a dark and damp cellar with a narrow passageway leading east, and a crawlway to the south. To the west is the bottom of a steep metal ramp which is unclimbable.

> east
Troll Room
This is a small room with passages off in all directions. Bloodstains and deep scratches (perhaps made by an axe) mar the walls.

You can see an elvish sword here.

> north
East-West Passage
This is a narrow east-west passageway. There is a narrow stairway leading down at the north end of the room.

> east
Round Room
You are in a circular room with passages off in eight directions.

You can see a steel box here.

> south
Engravings Cave
You are in a cave with strange engravings on the walls. A passage leads north, and stairs lead down.

> look
Engravings Cave
You are in a cave with strange engravings on the walls. A passage leads north, and stairs lead down.

> southeast
Riddle Room
This is a room which is bare on all sides. There is an exit down. To the east is a great door made of stone. Above the stone, the following words are written: 'No man shall enter this room without solving this riddle:

What is tall as a house,
round as a cup,
and all the king's horses can't draw it up?'

(Reply via 'ANSWER "answer"')

> answer "a well"
There is a loud rumble as the stone door swings open, revealing a passage to the east!

> east
Broom Closet
This is a former broom closet. The exits are to the east and west.

You can see a pearl necklace here.

> take necklace
Taken.

> east
Well Bottom
You are at the bottom of a well. The walls are too smooth to climb.

You can see a bucket here.

> enter bucket
You get into the bucket.

> pour water
The bucket becomes heavy with water and slowly rises to the top of the well, carrying you with it!

> look
Top of Well
You are at the top of a well. A bucket hangs from a rope here.

You can see a bucket here.

In the bucket you see yourself and a quantity of water.

> exit bucket
You get out of the bucket.

> east
Tea Room
This is a small room with a table. On the table are cakes of various sorts. Passages lead to the west, northwest, and east.

You can see a piece of paper, an eat-me eat-me cake, a blue blue cake, a red red cake, and an orange orange cake here.

> take blue cake
Taken.

> take red cake
Taken.

> eat eat-me cake
(first taking the eat-me cake)

Taken.

You eat the eat-me eat-me cake. It's quite tasty.

Suddenly the room seems to be getting much larger. Or maybe you are getting much smaller... In fact, you seem to have shrunk to the size of a mouse!

> look
Posts Room
This is a room with very large and very tall wooden posts in each corner. The room is otherwise featureless.

You can see a piece of paper and an orange orange cake here.

> east
Pool Room
This is a large room, one half of which is depressed. There is a large leak in the ceiling through which brown colored goop is falling. The only exit is to the west.

> throw red cake at pool
You throw the red red cake at the pool of goop. It hits!

The red cake sails through the air and lands with a splash in the pool of goop. As it dissolves, the pool begins to evaporate! In a few moments, the pool is gone, revealing something on the floor.

> take spices
Taken.

> west
Posts Room
This is a room with very large and very tall wooden posts in each corner. The room is otherwise featureless.

You can see a piece of paper and an orange orange cake here.

> eat blue cake
You eat the blue blue cake. It's quite tasty.

Suddenly, the room around you seems to be getting much smaller. Or maybe you are getting much bigger... In fact, you seem to have grown back to your normal size!

